1
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:04,026
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:47,194
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:47,277 --> 00:00:49,112
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:54,534
PREVIOUSLY

7
00:00:54,618 --> 00:00:57,287
[distorted voice] Detective Jin,
did you think the game was over?

8
00:00:57,371 --> 00:00:58,372
Round 2.

9
00:01:02,876 --> 00:01:04,419
[glass shattering]

10
00:01:05,754 --> 00:01:07,339
Detective Jin, you got lucky.

11
00:01:08,298 --> 00:01:11,093
For now, I think we should move
Detective Jin to a safe house.

12
00:01:11,176 --> 00:01:13,887
[Changun] Put Team 1 with him.
You can trust them.

13
00:01:15,055 --> 00:01:16,264
[scoffs]

14
00:01:17,599 --> 00:01:19,643
[Isoo] It's a box I've never seen before.

15
00:01:23,146 --> 00:01:24,523
[timer beeping]

16
00:01:24,606 --> 00:01:27,150
-What?
-It's a bomb!

17
00:01:27,234 --> 00:01:28,527
[tires screeching]

18
00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:30,028
What's going on?

19
00:01:30,112 --> 00:01:33,365
There's a bomb in the car.
Blast radius is 50... No, 100 meters.

20
00:01:33,448 --> 00:01:34,574
Take the wheel.

21
00:01:34,658 --> 00:01:36,034
[tires screeching]

22
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:38,203
[Hyera] Four minutes left.

23
00:01:38,745 --> 00:01:40,247
[Isoo] I know a place.

24
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:47,879
[siren blaring]

25
00:01:50,549 --> 00:01:51,675
[grunts]

26
00:01:55,429 --> 00:01:56,638
[grunts]

27
00:01:59,599 --> 00:02:01,184
[Hyera] There are people here. Be careful.

28
00:02:03,395 --> 00:02:06,106
[car horn honking]

29
00:02:06,189 --> 00:02:07,315
[grunts]

30
00:02:07,399 --> 00:02:10,152
[car horn honking]

31
00:02:13,447 --> 00:02:14,614
[tires screeching]

32
00:02:15,657 --> 00:02:17,993
-Detective Park, stop!
-[tires screech]

33
00:02:18,076 --> 00:02:19,536
[siren blaring]

34
00:02:22,164 --> 00:02:23,290
[tires screech]

35
00:02:29,921 --> 00:02:31,798
[tires screech]

36
00:02:32,799 --> 00:02:34,259
-Nine seconds.
-Open the door.

37
00:02:35,343 --> 00:02:36,845
-What?
-Open the door!

38
00:02:42,017 --> 00:02:43,351
[timer continues beeping]

39
00:02:50,275 --> 00:02:52,944
Three, two, one!

40
00:02:57,699 --> 00:02:58,700
[grunts]

41
00:02:59,242 --> 00:03:00,243
[heavy thud]

42
00:03:09,044 --> 00:03:10,128
[groans]

43
00:03:15,383 --> 00:03:18,428
[muffled explosion]
STYLE
::cue()

44
00:03:23,934 --> 00:03:25,685
[both panting]

45
00:03:31,316 --> 00:03:32,400
[Hyera grunts softly]

46
00:03:34,236 --> 00:03:35,612
[Isoo grunts]

47
00:03:35,695 --> 00:03:37,155
[Hyera grunts]

48
00:03:40,992 --> 00:03:41,993
[exhales sharply]

49
00:03:43,995 --> 00:03:45,997
[both continue panting]

50
00:03:46,873 --> 00:03:48,583
[car approaching]

51
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:50,544
-[tires screech]
-[car door opens]

52
00:03:50,627 --> 00:03:51,628
[Kyungjin] Bro!

53
00:03:55,173 --> 00:03:57,008
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

54
00:03:57,092 --> 00:03:58,843
That was way too close.

55
00:03:58,927 --> 00:03:59,928
Are you all right?

56
00:04:00,428 --> 00:04:01,429
Yes.

57
00:04:02,389 --> 00:04:05,559
We need a different location.
I don't know how far ahead they planned.

58
00:04:05,642 --> 00:04:07,602
[vehicles approaching]

59
00:04:09,479 --> 00:04:11,356
[siren blaring]

60
00:04:14,317 --> 00:04:16,653
Get Detective Jin out of here
before backup arrives.

61
00:04:17,153 --> 00:04:18,154
Understood.

62
00:04:20,782 --> 00:04:21,783
You're okay, right?

63
00:04:22,659 --> 00:04:23,660
Yes.

64
00:04:24,619 --> 00:04:25,954
[Junyoung exhales sharply]

65
00:04:27,539 --> 00:04:29,749
Violent Crimes' car exploded?

66
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:31,293
-Yes, sir.
-[gasps]

67
00:04:31,877 --> 00:04:34,129
You mean, the bomber came
to the police station

68
00:04:34,212 --> 00:04:36,423
and planted a bomb in our car?

69
00:04:36,506 --> 00:04:38,675
-[sighs softly]
-This is a nightmare.

70
00:04:39,551 --> 00:04:41,136
What are we going to do?

71
00:04:41,219 --> 00:04:43,388
The press is waiting.

72
00:04:44,055 --> 00:04:45,056
So what?

73
00:04:45,974 --> 00:04:48,268
-You handle it.
-Sir.

74
00:04:49,519 --> 00:04:52,188
Don't look at me.
Go out there and deal with it!

75
00:04:52,272 --> 00:04:53,982
[scoffs] I can't believe this.

76
00:04:54,065 --> 00:04:56,151
[breathing heavily]

77
00:04:56,234 --> 00:04:57,694
[♪ tense music playing]

78
00:04:57,777 --> 00:04:59,446
[reporters chattering]

79
00:05:01,156 --> 00:05:02,532
[reporter 1] Can you tell us
what happened?

80
00:05:02,616 --> 00:05:04,409
We heard a police vehicle had exploded.

81
00:05:04,492 --> 00:05:06,036
[reporter 2] Was
Detective Jin Isoo inside?

82
00:05:06,119 --> 00:05:07,162
[reporter 3] Any casualties?

83
00:05:07,245 --> 00:05:09,289
-[reporter 4] Did you catch them?
-Who's behind this?

84
00:05:09,372 --> 00:05:11,833
[reporters clamoring]

85
00:05:14,336 --> 00:05:15,337
[clamor subsides]

86
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:16,671
There are no casualties.

87
00:05:16,755 --> 00:05:20,592
We'll place this case under embargo
until the investigation is complete.

88
00:05:21,176 --> 00:05:22,510
[reporter 5] Embargo?

89
00:05:22,594 --> 00:05:24,804
We've already had
two large-scale explosions.

90
00:05:25,931 --> 00:05:28,391
We don't know what the culprit is after.

91
00:05:29,392 --> 00:05:30,977
We can't risk provoking them.

92
00:05:31,686 --> 00:05:32,687
Please cooperate.

93
00:05:32,771 --> 00:05:34,773
[clamor resumes]

94
00:05:52,457 --> 00:05:53,875
[Isoo sighs]

95
00:05:55,418 --> 00:05:57,295
Where are we?

96
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,882
The safest place we have right now.

97
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:05,261
Let's go inside.

98
00:06:15,981 --> 00:06:17,232
[Isoo sighs]

99
00:06:26,449 --> 00:06:28,243
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

100
00:06:28,326 --> 00:06:30,412
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

101
00:06:30,495 --> 00:06:32,455
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

102
00:06:32,539 --> 00:06:34,708
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

103
00:06:41,673 --> 00:06:44,009
What's with the decor here? Huh?
STYLE
::cue()

104
00:06:48,972 --> 00:06:50,015
MS. JOO HYERA

105
00:06:50,098 --> 00:06:52,100
-Is this Joo Hyera's place?
-Yeah.

106
00:06:52,183 --> 00:06:53,727
The bomber would never expect it.

107
00:06:53,810 --> 00:06:54,894
[Isoo] Yeah.

108
00:06:54,978 --> 00:06:57,272
I didn't expect it either.
I'm going to a hotel.

109
00:06:57,355 --> 00:06:58,481
Hey, come on. Why?

110
00:06:58,565 --> 00:07:00,692
Because she embarrassed me on national TV,

111
00:07:00,775 --> 00:07:03,737
and she keeps bossing me around
like she's our team leader.

112
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,155
Hey, Jin Isoo.

113
00:07:05,947 --> 00:07:09,617
She offered up her home to keep you safe.
Stop being so petty.

114
00:07:10,201 --> 00:07:11,828
[Kyungjin] He's right. You should rest.

115
00:07:11,911 --> 00:07:13,538
You've had a really stressful day.

116
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:15,665
Where's the bedroom?

117
00:07:15,749 --> 00:07:17,167
It's this way. Come on, bro.

118
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:18,585
[Isoo sighs in exasperation]

119
00:07:18,668 --> 00:07:20,211
[Kyungjin] God, we need a team leader.

120
00:07:20,295 --> 00:07:21,337
This way, bro.

121
00:07:23,339 --> 00:07:24,424
[Isoo sighs]

122
00:07:33,141 --> 00:07:34,142
[scoffs]

123
00:07:36,519 --> 00:07:38,646
That evil woman
likes cute things like this?

124
00:07:44,861 --> 00:07:46,654
[grunting]

125
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:50,617
Why're you lying on the floor?

126
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:52,494
I don't sleep in other people's beds.

127
00:07:52,577 --> 00:07:53,745
Go. I'm going to sleep.

128
00:08:05,965 --> 00:08:06,966
Night, bro.

129
00:08:11,346 --> 00:08:12,347
[door closes]

130
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,768
What about Isoo?

131
00:08:16,851 --> 00:08:18,144
He went to sleep.

132
00:08:18,228 --> 00:08:20,021
Okay. Good job today.

133
00:08:20,104 --> 00:08:22,148
You go back to the station.
I'll stay here.

134
00:08:22,232 --> 00:08:23,399
Got it.

135
00:08:27,195 --> 00:08:28,196
[sighs]

136
00:08:34,661 --> 00:08:36,204
MISSED CALL
JIWON

137
00:08:36,788 --> 00:08:37,956
[sighs]

138
00:08:43,586 --> 00:08:44,963
INCOMING CALL
JIWON

139
00:08:45,046 --> 00:08:46,297
[cell phone vibrating]

140
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:48,466
Hello? Jiwon, sorry--

141
00:08:48,550 --> 00:08:50,468
[Dr. Yoon] What happened?
Are you okay? Where are you?

142
00:08:51,052 --> 00:08:52,762
Uh, Jiwon.

143
00:08:52,846 --> 00:08:55,181
Calm down. One question at a time.

144
00:08:55,265 --> 00:08:58,560
How can I be calm?
A car exploded at the Hangang River.

145
00:08:59,144 --> 00:09:01,062
Isoo's unharmed.

146
00:09:01,146 --> 00:09:03,314
-We're now at a safe house, so--
-And you?

147
00:09:03,398 --> 00:09:04,399
What?

148
00:09:04,482 --> 00:09:06,276
Are you okay?

149
00:09:06,985 --> 00:09:08,903
I was really worried.

150
00:09:12,031 --> 00:09:14,826
Yes, I'm completely fine.

151
00:09:15,451 --> 00:09:16,619
[sighs in relief]

152
00:09:20,290 --> 00:09:21,916
Do you know how scared I was?

153
00:09:23,710 --> 00:09:25,753
Who on earth would do something like this?

154
00:09:26,504 --> 00:09:27,755
Exactly.

155
00:09:28,673 --> 00:09:31,843
This is the third incident now.
I'm sure we'll find some evidence.

156
00:09:31,926 --> 00:09:35,346
I need Team 2 to go over the footage
from the launch event again.

157
00:09:35,430 --> 00:09:37,640
Let me know if you see
any suspicious movements.

158
00:09:37,724 --> 00:09:39,267
[in English] Okay. [in Korean] Come on.

159
00:09:39,893 --> 00:09:41,019
-[detective 1] Okay.
-[detective 2] Okay.

160
00:09:44,898 --> 00:09:46,983
Let's check
the parking lot security footage.

161
00:09:47,066 --> 00:09:48,067
Got it.

162
00:09:50,945 --> 00:09:51,946
[sighs softly]

163
00:09:53,114 --> 00:09:54,115
[mouse clicks]

164
00:09:54,199 --> 00:09:56,117
[♪ suspenseful music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

165
00:10:07,170 --> 00:10:08,213
[music fades]

166
00:10:20,016 --> 00:10:21,267
[groans softly]

167
00:10:21,351 --> 00:10:22,352
[cell phone vibrates]

168
00:10:29,984 --> 00:10:31,194
[distorted voice, in English] Final Round.

169
00:10:31,277 --> 00:10:33,488
[♪ foreboding music playing]

170
00:10:41,746 --> 00:10:43,998
[in Korean] Come alone.
He'll blow up if I see anyone else.

171
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:46,709
You know where this is.

172
00:10:50,296 --> 00:10:51,297
MR. CHOI

173
00:10:51,881 --> 00:10:53,299
[line ringing]

174
00:10:58,846 --> 00:11:01,224
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed...

175
00:11:01,307 --> 00:11:04,644
[music swells, fades]

176
00:11:08,982 --> 00:11:10,275
[keyboard clacks]

177
00:11:11,150 --> 00:11:12,902
[sighs heavily] Did you find anything?

178
00:11:13,486 --> 00:11:14,487
No.

179
00:11:14,988 --> 00:11:16,906
No one approached the vehicle.

180
00:11:18,741 --> 00:11:20,785
Then how did they put the bomb in there?

181
00:11:21,744 --> 00:11:23,371
When was the vehicle last used?

182
00:11:23,454 --> 00:11:24,789
Three days ago.

183
00:11:26,624 --> 00:11:28,751
Let's check the nearby dashcams
in the morning.

184
00:11:28,835 --> 00:11:29,961
Okay.

185
00:11:30,044 --> 00:11:31,045
By the way,

186
00:11:32,255 --> 00:11:33,548
what about Park Gyeongtae?

187
00:11:33,631 --> 00:11:35,508
[♪ ominous music plays]

188
00:11:38,886 --> 00:11:41,806
We've been watching him,
but he never left his house.

189
00:11:41,889 --> 00:11:43,224
[sighs]

190
00:11:43,808 --> 00:11:45,935
My team will retrieve
the vehicle tomorrow.

191
00:11:47,061 --> 00:11:48,771
-Go get some shut-eye.
-Okay.

192
00:11:52,567 --> 00:11:53,693
[sighs softly]

193
00:12:04,412 --> 00:12:05,455
[sighs heavily]

194
00:12:16,549 --> 00:12:17,759
[cell phone snaps shut]

195
00:12:29,854 --> 00:12:31,856
[♪ gripping music playing]

196
00:12:36,402 --> 00:12:37,820
[shower running]

197
00:13:07,225 --> 00:13:09,185
NEARBY PARKED VEHICLE RECORDS

198
00:13:09,268 --> 00:13:10,520
[music fades]

199
00:13:12,563 --> 00:13:14,857
[line connects, ringing]

200
00:13:16,359 --> 00:13:18,903
Yes, sir.
Sorry for disturbing you so early.

201
00:13:18,986 --> 00:13:20,571
I couldn't reach you yesterday.

202
00:13:21,948 --> 00:13:24,117
You parked in front
of a Violent Crimes vehicle.

203
00:13:24,951 --> 00:13:27,078
I need to check your dashcam footage.

204
00:13:27,662 --> 00:13:30,373
Yes, please call me when you arrive.
I'll come up to get it.

205
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,501
[line disconnects]

206
00:13:34,293 --> 00:13:36,671
-I'll contact the rest of the list.
-Okay.

207
00:13:50,768 --> 00:13:52,311
Sorry, I left on my own.

208
00:13:53,813 --> 00:13:55,356
Even if I end up dead,

209
00:13:56,107 --> 00:13:57,483
you guys are not at fault.

210
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:01,487
Park Junyoung, Choi Kyungjin...

211
00:14:02,655 --> 00:14:03,865
Thanks for everything.

212
00:14:04,615 --> 00:14:06,784
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

213
00:14:07,368 --> 00:14:08,870
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

214
00:14:08,953 --> 00:14:09,954
-Good luck.
-Thanks.

215
00:14:14,292 --> 00:14:15,293
Hey, here you go.

216
00:14:15,376 --> 00:14:16,919
-Thank you.
-Take care.

217
00:14:17,003 --> 00:14:18,004
Yes, sir.
STYLE
::cue()

218
00:14:23,384 --> 00:14:27,471
THIRD INCIDENT
POLICE VEHICLE BOMB ATTACK

219
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:32,768
HIGH-YIELD AMMONIUM NITRATE IED

220
00:14:32,852 --> 00:14:34,437
100-METER BLAST RADIUS

221
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:36,147
[music intensifies]

222
00:14:43,613 --> 00:14:44,780
[♪ music fades]

223
00:15:00,338 --> 00:15:01,589
[♪ tense music playing]

224
00:15:02,882 --> 00:15:04,133
[sighs in exasperation]

225
00:15:08,221 --> 00:15:11,140
[line connects, ringing]

226
00:15:11,224 --> 00:15:14,602
[cell phone vibrating]

227
00:15:16,854 --> 00:15:18,356
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed...

228
00:15:18,439 --> 00:15:20,566
[sighs wearily] Isoo.

229
00:15:24,362 --> 00:15:25,738
[cell phone vibrating]

230
00:15:26,239 --> 00:15:27,240
Hello?

231
00:15:27,990 --> 00:15:28,991
What?

232
00:15:30,159 --> 00:15:31,160
Understood.

233
00:15:33,204 --> 00:15:35,206
-What's wrong?
-Isoo disappeared.

234
00:15:36,707 --> 00:15:39,085
-Did he take Detective Park's car?
-I think so.

235
00:15:40,419 --> 00:15:43,381
-I'll head out now. You track him down.
-Got it.

236
00:15:47,468 --> 00:15:49,720
[engine revving]

237
00:16:01,732 --> 00:16:04,193
There he is.
Please track license plate 9832.

238
00:16:04,277 --> 00:16:05,278
[officer] Got it.

239
00:16:16,872 --> 00:16:18,040
[cell phone ringing]

240
00:16:19,250 --> 00:16:21,877
-[Kyungjin] Ma'am.
-Yes, where's Detective Jin?

241
00:16:21,961 --> 00:16:24,505
Near his family estate.
The address is 251 Pyeongjin-dong.

242
00:16:24,588 --> 00:16:26,674
I'll head over there, so keep me updated.

243
00:16:26,757 --> 00:16:29,093
-And let Detective Park know, too.
-Yes, ma'am.

244
00:16:42,898 --> 00:16:44,817
[♪ foreboding music playing]

245
00:16:54,201 --> 00:16:55,619
[panting]

246
00:16:55,703 --> 00:16:57,330
What are you doing here?

247
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:02,001
I got a DM.

248
00:17:02,084 --> 00:17:04,628
I was told to come here and film you die.

249
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,631
GO FILM HIM DIE
BE THERE, OR ELSE

250
00:17:07,715 --> 00:17:08,716
It's my mom.

251
00:17:11,677 --> 00:17:12,678
[cell phone vibrates]

252
00:17:14,430 --> 00:17:16,599
[distorted voice] Head inside together.

253
00:17:18,476 --> 00:17:19,727
We're being watched.

254
00:17:21,729 --> 00:17:22,730
Let's go inside.

255
00:17:29,070 --> 00:17:30,071
Mr. Choi!

256
00:17:42,958 --> 00:17:44,043
[cell phone vibrates]

257
00:17:45,753 --> 00:17:47,171
[distorted voice] Turn on the camera.

258
00:17:47,254 --> 00:17:49,173
Unless you want to see your mom die.

259
00:17:50,007 --> 00:17:52,093
[♪ enthralling music playing]

260
00:18:21,747 --> 00:18:22,873
[cell phone vibrates]

261
00:18:23,749 --> 00:18:24,917
[music fades]

262
00:18:26,961 --> 00:18:27,962
Turn around.

263
00:18:30,172 --> 00:18:32,091
[♪ suspenseful music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

264
00:18:45,354 --> 00:18:48,482
[gasps in fear] Detective! Detective Jin!

265
00:18:48,566 --> 00:18:49,567
Over here.

266
00:18:59,827 --> 00:19:03,581
There's a bomb in the car.
Blast radius is 50... No, 100 meters.

267
00:19:06,333 --> 00:19:07,334
[Isoo] Follow me.

268
00:19:10,755 --> 00:19:12,882
[grunts] There's a bunker here.

269
00:19:13,507 --> 00:19:14,550
[gasps in disbelief]

270
00:19:15,426 --> 00:19:16,552
[timer beeping]

271
00:19:17,344 --> 00:19:18,971
[clangs]

272
00:19:19,054 --> 00:19:20,389
[metallic creak]

273
00:19:21,390 --> 00:19:22,767
-[cell phone vibrates]
-Hello?

274
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:24,643
He's at Jin Myeongchul's house.

275
00:19:24,727 --> 00:19:26,395
I think Jin Isoo has been set up.

276
00:19:26,479 --> 00:19:28,063
[sighs]

277
00:19:28,147 --> 00:19:30,357
Please alert local police
and emergency services.

278
00:19:30,441 --> 00:19:31,525
I will.

279
00:19:31,609 --> 00:19:33,569
-Be careful.
-Yes, sir.

280
00:19:36,405 --> 00:19:38,032
[Hyeonwoo panting frantically]

281
00:19:38,991 --> 00:19:40,826
[timer continues beeping]

282
00:19:40,910 --> 00:19:43,037
[continues panting]

283
00:19:51,670 --> 00:19:53,297
It should've gone off by now.

284
00:20:05,267 --> 00:20:06,393
[mouse clicking]

285
00:20:08,687 --> 00:20:09,688
[camera chimes]

286
00:20:11,899 --> 00:20:13,692
[Hyeonwoo breathing heavily]

287
00:20:19,365 --> 00:20:20,825
[keyboard clacking]

288
00:20:22,159 --> 00:20:24,245
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

289
00:20:30,626 --> 00:20:32,211
That bastard was bluffing.

290
00:20:33,712 --> 00:20:34,713
[scoffs]

291
00:20:38,342 --> 00:20:39,385
[gasps in horror]

292
00:20:39,468 --> 00:20:40,761
Detective!

293
00:20:40,845 --> 00:20:42,221
[panting frantically]

294
00:20:44,932 --> 00:20:46,350
[timer beeping]

295
00:20:47,226 --> 00:20:48,811
[music intensifies, fades]

296
00:20:54,817 --> 00:20:56,026
[tires screech]

297
00:20:58,153 --> 00:20:59,238
[engine shuts off]

298
00:21:02,825 --> 00:21:04,034
[explosion]

299
00:21:04,118 --> 00:21:06,036
[♪ tense music playing]

300
00:21:12,126 --> 00:21:13,127
Detective Jin!

301
00:21:15,212 --> 00:21:16,463
Jin Isoo, where are you?

302
00:21:38,193 --> 00:21:40,779
-[footsteps approaching]
-[Isoo sighs in relief]

303
00:21:40,863 --> 00:21:42,531
[coughs] Over here.

304
00:21:45,409 --> 00:21:47,661
Are you okay? What happened?

305
00:21:48,495 --> 00:21:50,331
[panting]

306
00:21:51,123 --> 00:21:52,875
Why is the Assistant Director here?

307
00:21:54,084 --> 00:21:56,587
It's a long story.
Let's get out of here first.

308
00:21:56,670 --> 00:21:59,089
[hurried footsteps approaching]

309
00:21:59,173 --> 00:22:00,174
Hey.

310
00:22:01,550 --> 00:22:02,551
You okay?

311
00:22:04,678 --> 00:22:06,138
[sighs wearily]

312
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:07,806
You asshole!

313
00:22:09,433 --> 00:22:10,434
You...

314
00:22:10,935 --> 00:22:12,436
If something had happened to you...

315
00:22:12,519 --> 00:22:14,897
I didn't have a choice.
Let's get out of here first.

316
00:22:16,649 --> 00:22:17,650
[grunts in frustration]

317
00:22:34,416 --> 00:22:37,044
[♪ suspenseful music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

318
00:22:41,966 --> 00:22:43,509
[sirens blaring]

319
00:22:48,764 --> 00:22:50,057
[brakes squeal]

320
00:22:51,642 --> 00:22:53,310
[Isoo] It was because of this.

321
00:23:00,025 --> 00:23:01,402
But he wasn't here?

322
00:23:02,611 --> 00:23:03,612
No.

323
00:23:04,780 --> 00:23:06,532
[sighs] Then what could've happened?

324
00:23:07,282 --> 00:23:08,701
[Hyera] Was he taken somewhere else?

325
00:23:09,243 --> 00:23:10,869
Maybe the photo was just a bait.

326
00:23:11,704 --> 00:23:13,622
The photo was definitely taken here.

327
00:23:17,501 --> 00:23:18,627
[Kyungjin] Chairman Choi is here.

328
00:23:20,921 --> 00:23:22,339
-[Isoo] Mr. Choi.
-Yes.

329
00:23:22,923 --> 00:23:24,008
Are you all right?

330
00:23:24,591 --> 00:23:25,676
Did you get hurt?

331
00:23:25,759 --> 00:23:27,511
What about you?

332
00:23:27,594 --> 00:23:28,721
Where were you?

333
00:23:29,304 --> 00:23:31,140
I was traveling by helicopter.

334
00:23:31,223 --> 00:23:33,142
Then how did you know to come here?

335
00:23:33,225 --> 00:23:36,520
You didn't answer when I called you back,
so I contacted Detective Choi.

336
00:23:37,187 --> 00:23:38,564
[sighs softly]

337
00:23:42,818 --> 00:23:44,236
You should call your mother.

338
00:23:48,157 --> 00:23:50,200
[line connects, ringing]

339
00:23:51,535 --> 00:23:54,496
Hello? Mom, where are you?
Why didn't you answer your phone?

340
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:56,165
At the sauna?

341
00:23:56,915 --> 00:23:58,959
God, Mom! I really can't with you.

342
00:23:59,043 --> 00:24:00,544
-I'm hanging up.
-[line disconnects]

343
00:24:01,128 --> 00:24:02,921
So this was just a deepfake.

344
00:24:03,756 --> 00:24:06,467
Then why bomb this place?
Using a fake photo, no less.

345
00:24:08,719 --> 00:24:10,095
To kill me.

346
00:24:15,392 --> 00:24:17,061
We should go. It's too dangerous.

347
00:24:17,644 --> 00:24:18,729
[Hyera] Wait.

348
00:24:21,732 --> 00:24:23,358
You said the bomber's watching.

349
00:24:24,902 --> 00:24:27,279
[ticking]

350
00:24:29,406 --> 00:24:31,200
[♪ tense music playing]

351
00:24:31,283 --> 00:24:33,535
[onlookers murmuring]

352
00:24:46,048 --> 00:24:48,967
[♪ ominous music plays]

353
00:24:49,051 --> 00:24:50,928
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

354
00:24:51,011 --> 00:24:54,598
The unexploded bomb was defused on site,
and it's currently being analyzed.

355
00:24:54,681 --> 00:24:55,682
FORENSICS

356
00:24:55,766 --> 00:24:57,726
[♪ soft suspenseful music playing]

357
00:25:04,525 --> 00:25:06,902
[Hyera] Jang Hyeonwoo is hiding out
at a nearby motel.

358
00:25:09,029 --> 00:25:11,240
[coughing]

359
00:25:11,824 --> 00:25:13,575
And I've relocated Detective Jin.

360
00:25:14,535 --> 00:25:15,661
Where?

361
00:25:15,744 --> 00:25:17,246
[birds chirping]

362
00:25:18,997 --> 00:25:21,416
[♪ serene music playing]

363
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,252
[Isoo exclaims in satisfaction]

364
00:25:23,335 --> 00:25:25,045
I haven't been over in so long.

365
00:25:25,129 --> 00:25:26,505
[grunts]

366
00:25:29,174 --> 00:25:31,718
[Mr. Choi] Go wash up.
I'll make you something to eat.

367
00:25:31,802 --> 00:25:33,095
In a minute.

368
00:25:33,887 --> 00:25:35,681
[chuckles] Quickly, come on.

369
00:25:36,181 --> 00:25:37,641
There you go. [grunts]

370
00:25:38,851 --> 00:25:39,977
[exhales deeply]

371
00:25:43,272 --> 00:25:44,273
[chuckles softly]

372
00:25:46,650 --> 00:25:48,610
[Isoo exclaims in satisfaction]

373
00:25:48,694 --> 00:25:51,530
This house seems too small
for the chairman of the Hansu Group.

374
00:25:51,613 --> 00:25:52,990
Do you want a bigger place?

375
00:25:53,866 --> 00:25:55,242
I like it here.

376
00:25:55,325 --> 00:25:56,493
And I like you, Mr. Choi.

377
00:25:56,577 --> 00:25:58,162
[chuckles]

378
00:25:58,245 --> 00:25:59,246
Have a seat.

379
00:26:00,330 --> 00:26:01,540
[sighs contentedly]

380
00:26:05,043 --> 00:26:06,837
CHOI JEONGHUN

381
00:26:07,588 --> 00:26:08,797
Are you unwell?

382
00:26:10,299 --> 00:26:12,885
No, it's just a little indigestion.

383
00:26:13,844 --> 00:26:15,554
Did you get it checked out?

384
00:26:15,637 --> 00:26:16,638
I will.

385
00:26:17,264 --> 00:26:18,265
Go on.

386
00:26:19,266 --> 00:26:20,851
[chair clatters]

387
00:26:22,603 --> 00:26:24,188
[breathes deeply]

388
00:26:24,271 --> 00:26:25,898
I haven't had porridge in a while.

389
00:26:27,191 --> 00:26:28,233
Mmm.

390
00:26:28,317 --> 00:26:29,985
-[Mr. Choi] How is it?
-It's seasoned perfectly.
STYLE
::cue()

391
00:26:30,068 --> 00:26:31,445
-Just as I expected.
-[chuckles]

392
00:26:31,528 --> 00:26:34,865
Mmm. Mmm.

393
00:26:34,948 --> 00:26:37,117
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

394
00:26:50,839 --> 00:26:52,216
We got a partial print.

395
00:26:52,716 --> 00:26:54,384
Submit it for expedited analysis.

396
00:26:54,468 --> 00:26:55,719
It's really urgent.

397
00:26:56,511 --> 00:26:58,513
-Did they find something?
-[Hyera] Yes.

398
00:26:58,597 --> 00:27:00,432
A partial print. It'll take a while.

399
00:27:02,059 --> 00:27:03,060
FOURTH INCIDENT

400
00:27:05,062 --> 00:27:07,648
Four bomb attacks,
but only one partial fingerprint.

401
00:27:08,232 --> 00:27:11,568
We should've found something
at the event site or the parking lot.

402
00:27:12,194 --> 00:27:13,862
Anything on the security footage?

403
00:27:15,405 --> 00:27:18,784
We checked all the parking lot cameras
and dashcams.

404
00:27:18,867 --> 00:27:20,953
Everything up to two days
before the incident.

405
00:27:24,831 --> 00:27:26,041
[exhales heavily]

406
00:27:30,545 --> 00:27:31,838
It wasn't here.

407
00:27:32,923 --> 00:27:34,466
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

408
00:27:35,842 --> 00:27:39,221
No one's bold enough
to plant a bomb at a police station.

409
00:27:41,556 --> 00:27:44,184
-You went to the first site in that car?
-Yes.

410
00:27:45,394 --> 00:27:47,312
They lured you there to plant the bomb.

411
00:27:49,106 --> 00:27:50,565
I'll get their security footage.

412
00:27:58,740 --> 00:28:00,409
ANONYMOUS TIPSTER

413
00:28:01,743 --> 00:28:02,828
[Isoo sighs]

414
00:28:04,621 --> 00:28:06,164
Who could be behind all this?

415
00:28:08,166 --> 00:28:09,334
[sighs deeply]

416
00:28:09,418 --> 00:28:10,836
Yeah, who could it be?

417
00:28:10,919 --> 00:28:12,379
Who would want me...

418
00:28:14,423 --> 00:28:15,966
[high-pitched ringing]

419
00:28:16,049 --> 00:28:18,427
[♪ pensive music playing]

420
00:28:20,137 --> 00:28:21,555
[Junyoung] Don't touch that!

421
00:28:21,638 --> 00:28:23,682
-[exhales, grunts]
-[timer beeping rapidly]

422
00:28:23,765 --> 00:28:26,101
[distorted voice] Come alone.
He'll blow up if I see anyone else.

423
00:28:27,352 --> 00:28:28,520
[groans in pain]

424
00:28:28,603 --> 00:28:30,188
-[muffled bang]
-[high-pitched ringing continues]

425
00:28:30,272 --> 00:28:31,982
-[Mr. Choi] What's wrong?
-Detective!

426
00:28:32,065 --> 00:28:33,775
-[glass shattering]
-[muffled explosion]

427
00:28:33,859 --> 00:28:35,235
[Isoo exhales sharply]

428
00:28:36,695 --> 00:28:37,988
[distant tinkling]

429
00:28:38,071 --> 00:28:39,239
[grunts in pain]

430
00:28:40,365 --> 00:28:42,200
-[music stops]
-Drink this.

431
00:28:43,785 --> 00:28:44,786
[grunts]

432
00:28:45,328 --> 00:28:46,329
[gulps]

433
00:28:47,914 --> 00:28:49,041
[exhales shakily]

434
00:28:49,958 --> 00:28:50,959
Are you all right?

435
00:28:51,543 --> 00:28:52,544
[panting] Yeah.

436
00:28:53,045 --> 00:28:54,379
I just...

437
00:28:54,463 --> 00:28:55,964
couldn't breathe for a second.

438
00:28:56,673 --> 00:28:57,799
[sighs]

439
00:28:57,883 --> 00:28:59,634
You should go to the hospital.

440
00:28:59,718 --> 00:29:00,761
[pants]

441
00:29:01,428 --> 00:29:02,679
If you go first.

442
00:29:03,513 --> 00:29:05,807
[pants] I'm fine.

443
00:29:09,352 --> 00:29:11,855
[exhales deeply]
I really don't know who it could be.

444
00:29:15,692 --> 00:29:18,070
But why make it so complicated?

445
00:29:18,862 --> 00:29:21,823
Planting bombs at four locations
and even using a deepfake?

446
00:29:23,158 --> 00:29:24,993
Why not just plant it at your house?

447
00:29:33,293 --> 00:29:34,836
[Seungju] It probably isn't revenge.

448
00:29:36,004 --> 00:29:37,130
The Isoo I know

449
00:29:37,923 --> 00:29:40,884
would never make someone
want revenge this badly.

450
00:29:41,927 --> 00:29:42,928
It might be

451
00:29:43,553 --> 00:29:45,514
driven by desire.

452
00:29:48,266 --> 00:29:50,393
-[pops]
-[clangs]

453
00:29:51,812 --> 00:29:53,188
-[timer beeps]
-[explosion]

454
00:29:56,441 --> 00:29:58,068
[gasps] Mr. Choi.

455
00:29:59,236 --> 00:30:00,779
You know my dad's house.

456
00:30:00,862 --> 00:30:02,656
Do you remember it had a bunker?

457
00:30:02,739 --> 00:30:04,074
Yes, of course.

458
00:30:05,075 --> 00:30:07,661
The bomb went off in there,
which is how I survived.

459
00:30:08,161 --> 00:30:09,788
But it blew a hole in the floor.
STYLE
::cue()

460
00:30:16,628 --> 00:30:18,964
I got the footage
from Hansu Department Store.

461
00:30:23,093 --> 00:30:24,344
[keyboard clacking]

462
00:30:32,227 --> 00:30:33,895
[mouse clicking]

463
00:30:37,691 --> 00:30:40,485
[sighs] We won't be able to see anything.

464
00:30:43,155 --> 00:30:44,865
We got a match on the fingerprint.

465
00:30:47,742 --> 00:30:51,413
Jang Hyeonsuk. No criminal record.
He works in R&amp;D at Mirae Electronics.

466
00:30:51,496 --> 00:30:52,497
JANG HYEONSUK

467
00:30:54,249 --> 00:30:56,501
-Should we go bring him in?
-Yes.

468
00:30:56,585 --> 00:30:58,253
-Let's go.
-Right.

469
00:31:02,924 --> 00:31:04,885
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

470
00:31:07,512 --> 00:31:09,556
FIRST INCIDENT
HANSU DEPARTMENT STORE

471
00:31:09,639 --> 00:31:12,392
[Hyera] The first bomb
had a simple design.

472
00:31:12,475 --> 00:31:14,019
Its target was Jin Isoo.

473
00:31:17,898 --> 00:31:18,982
SECOND INCIDENT

474
00:31:19,858 --> 00:31:21,443
The second bomb...

475
00:31:21,943 --> 00:31:23,236
[glass shattering]

476
00:31:23,570 --> 00:31:25,655
It was used to prove they meant business.

477
00:31:26,865 --> 00:31:28,283
THIRD INCIDENT
POLICE VEHICLE

478
00:31:28,867 --> 00:31:30,869
The third bomb...

479
00:31:35,415 --> 00:31:37,667
[muffled explosion]

480
00:31:37,751 --> 00:31:41,129
We need a different location.
I don't know how far ahead they planned.

481
00:31:41,713 --> 00:31:44,716
It sent Jin Isoo to a safe house
and isolated him.

482
00:31:44,799 --> 00:31:45,800
FOURTH INCIDENT

483
00:31:45,884 --> 00:31:47,385
The fourth bomb...

484
00:31:47,969 --> 00:31:49,888
It finally tried to kill Jin Isoo,

485
00:31:49,971 --> 00:31:52,933
but failed because there was a bunker
in the house?

486
00:31:56,686 --> 00:31:57,896
[inhales deeply]

487
00:31:58,521 --> 00:32:00,398
No, that's not it.

488
00:32:08,156 --> 00:32:11,743
There were three explosions.
How could there be no casualties?

489
00:32:13,245 --> 00:32:15,163
[music intensifies, fades]

490
00:32:20,919 --> 00:32:23,129
The bomber wasn't trying to kill Jin Isoo.

491
00:32:28,218 --> 00:32:29,219
[door slides open]

492
00:32:29,803 --> 00:32:31,179
[Mr. Choi exhales deeply]

493
00:32:31,263 --> 00:32:32,305
[sharp gasp]

494
00:32:33,098 --> 00:32:35,475
Do you seriously only own suits?

495
00:32:36,059 --> 00:32:38,061
I even go hiking in a suit.

496
00:32:38,561 --> 00:32:40,188
God, you're so buttoned-up.

497
00:32:40,272 --> 00:32:42,148
It's my fashion philosophy.

498
00:32:42,899 --> 00:32:45,902
By the way, where are you going?

499
00:32:46,486 --> 00:32:49,739
[inhales] I think
I know what the bombers are after.

500
00:32:50,699 --> 00:32:52,784
It could be dangerous.

501
00:32:53,535 --> 00:32:55,120
That looks even more dangerous.

502
00:32:57,497 --> 00:32:58,832
This is great!

503
00:32:59,624 --> 00:33:00,709
It's unique.
STYLE
::cue()

504
00:33:05,005 --> 00:33:06,798
They weren't trying to kill me.

505
00:33:08,174 --> 00:33:09,551
It was all a ruse.

506
00:33:10,218 --> 00:33:11,886
I'll go catch them.

507
00:33:13,930 --> 00:33:15,056
[sighs]

508
00:33:15,765 --> 00:33:17,892
-[cell phone vibrates]
-Hello?

509
00:33:17,976 --> 00:33:19,519
Yes, Director. This is Joo Hyera.

510
00:33:20,312 --> 00:33:23,273
Whose idea was it to do a feature
on Detective Jin Isoo?

511
00:33:23,356 --> 00:33:25,900
It was Assistant Director Jang Hyeonwoo.

512
00:33:25,984 --> 00:33:27,819
He said he's a fan of Detective Jin.

513
00:33:27,902 --> 00:33:29,529
Right. Okay.

514
00:33:29,612 --> 00:33:31,364
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

515
00:33:32,324 --> 00:33:33,616
-[cell phone snaps shut]
-That was random.

516
00:33:33,700 --> 00:33:35,452
[line connects, ringing]

517
00:33:36,536 --> 00:33:38,371
Hello, this is Joo Hyera.

518
00:33:39,456 --> 00:33:42,208
Could you check
if Jang Hyeonwoo is inside his room?

519
00:33:42,292 --> 00:33:43,460
Yes, right away.

520
00:33:44,336 --> 00:33:45,462
[line disconnects]

521
00:33:55,972 --> 00:33:57,390
[keyboard clacking]

522
00:34:00,810 --> 00:34:02,562
[mouse clicks]

523
00:34:03,855 --> 00:34:05,565
[♪ tense music playing]

524
00:34:09,027 --> 00:34:10,153
[keyboard key clacks]

525
00:34:23,041 --> 00:34:24,959
JANG HYEONSUK

526
00:34:25,043 --> 00:34:26,920
SIBLING JANG HYEONWOO

527
00:34:34,886 --> 00:34:36,137
[digital beeping]

528
00:34:40,558 --> 00:34:42,352
He used the van to block him from view.

529
00:34:43,144 --> 00:34:44,145
Jang Hyeonwoo.

530
00:34:45,063 --> 00:34:46,064
Jang Hyeonsuk.

531
00:34:49,234 --> 00:34:50,735
PYEONGJIN-DONG ESTATE BOMB ATTACK

532
00:34:50,819 --> 00:34:52,278
251 PYEONGJIN-DONG, SEONGBUK-GU

533
00:34:54,406 --> 00:34:57,617
251 PYEONGJIN-DONG, SEONGBUK-GU

534
00:34:57,701 --> 00:34:59,119
[cell phone vibrating]

535
00:35:01,287 --> 00:35:02,288
Hello?

536
00:35:02,872 --> 00:35:04,457
Jang Hyeonwoo's not here.

537
00:35:19,639 --> 00:35:20,974
[cell phone vibrating]

538
00:35:22,559 --> 00:35:23,601
Detective Park.

539
00:35:25,729 --> 00:35:26,813
[Junyoung clicks tongue]

540
00:35:27,814 --> 00:35:31,568
We can't locate Jang Hyeonsuk.
He hasn't shown up for work either.

541
00:35:32,444 --> 00:35:34,821
-Meet me at Jin Myeongchul's house.
-[Junyoung] Got it.

542
00:35:37,490 --> 00:35:38,491
Let's go.
STYLE
::cue()

543
00:35:50,170 --> 00:35:52,088
[♪ foreboding music playing]

544
00:35:56,509 --> 00:35:57,510
[tires screech]

545
00:36:02,599 --> 00:36:03,600
Joo Hyera?

546
00:36:04,809 --> 00:36:06,311
What's with the badass look?

547
00:36:06,394 --> 00:36:07,771
It's for mobility.

548
00:36:08,646 --> 00:36:10,690
And you? Are you Indiana Jones?

549
00:36:12,317 --> 00:36:14,235
[sighs sarcastically]
Too bad I don't have a whip.

550
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:17,238
-What made you come here?
-[inhales deeply]

551
00:36:17,322 --> 00:36:22,035
I just couldn't figure out how
they planted the bomb inside the house.

552
00:36:22,744 --> 00:36:24,788
Unless the Assistant Director
brought it in.

553
00:36:27,957 --> 00:36:29,626
[♪ dramatic music playing]

554
00:36:33,838 --> 00:36:35,298
[panting frantically]

555
00:36:36,674 --> 00:36:37,675
I can do this.

556
00:36:37,759 --> 00:36:38,760
I can do it.

557
00:36:39,636 --> 00:36:40,762
I can do it.

558
00:36:48,561 --> 00:36:50,188
Detective! Detective Jin!

559
00:36:53,775 --> 00:36:54,984
[digital beeping]

560
00:36:56,402 --> 00:36:57,904
[timer beeping]

561
00:36:57,987 --> 00:36:59,656
What about you? How did you know?

562
00:36:59,739 --> 00:37:02,200
We got a fingerprint off the bomb
by the entrance.

563
00:37:02,283 --> 00:37:03,743
It's Jang Hyeonwoo's brother.

564
00:37:03,827 --> 00:37:07,163
They used to live at this address.
And their mother died five years ago.

565
00:37:07,747 --> 00:37:08,873
Oh...

566
00:37:08,957 --> 00:37:11,334
-You're actually pretty sharp.
-[scoffs]

567
00:37:12,210 --> 00:37:14,170
Their target was the bunker, right?

568
00:37:14,254 --> 00:37:15,255
Yes.

569
00:37:15,338 --> 00:37:18,091
The whole thing was a setup
to blow up that place.

570
00:37:18,174 --> 00:37:20,635
Because I'm the only one who can open it.

571
00:37:21,302 --> 00:37:24,138
-[grunts] There's a bunker here.
-[clangs]

572
00:37:24,222 --> 00:37:25,849
[metallic creak]

573
00:37:25,932 --> 00:37:27,809
-[gasps in disbelief]
-Mr. Choi told me

574
00:37:27,892 --> 00:37:30,103
that an extremely
wealthy family used to live here.

575
00:37:31,020 --> 00:37:34,858
When their business went under, they sold
the house to my dad 30 years ago,

576
00:37:35,692 --> 00:37:37,360
but for the last two years or so,

577
00:37:37,443 --> 00:37:40,154
that family kept trying
to buy the house back.

578
00:37:40,738 --> 00:37:41,865
What's in this house?

579
00:37:42,448 --> 00:37:44,784
Good question. Shall we go find out?

580
00:38:04,804 --> 00:38:06,306
[muffled voices]

581
00:38:06,389 --> 00:38:07,724
[thudding footsteps]

582
00:38:09,183 --> 00:38:10,351
[Hyeonsuk] Hey, I'll grab that end. Move.

583
00:38:11,895 --> 00:38:13,229
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

584
00:38:13,813 --> 00:38:15,231
[whispering] Looks like
they're already here.

585
00:38:19,777 --> 00:38:22,572
-[muffled clattering]
-[muffled chatter continues]

586
00:38:28,077 --> 00:38:29,454
[Hyeonsuk] Okay, lift on three.

587
00:38:31,623 --> 00:38:33,416
[Hyeonwoo and Hyeonsuk grunting]

588
00:38:33,499 --> 00:38:35,501
[Hyeonsuk] Hey, I'll grab that end. Move.

589
00:38:37,587 --> 00:38:39,213
-Lift. One, two, three.
-[both grunting]

590
00:38:40,882 --> 00:38:42,342
-Hyeonsuk!
-Properly.

591
00:38:42,425 --> 00:38:44,218
I told you to bring a dolly.

592
00:38:44,302 --> 00:38:45,803
-Okay, okay.
-It's so heavy.

593
00:38:45,887 --> 00:38:48,681
Think this is gold?
How much would it be worth?

594
00:38:48,765 --> 00:38:51,100
Enough to live our dreams, of course.
STYLE
::cue()

595
00:38:51,184 --> 00:38:52,268
[both chuckle]

596
00:38:52,352 --> 00:38:55,104
[Hyeonsuk] I'm going to throw
my resignation right in my manager's face.

597
00:38:56,814 --> 00:38:57,815
You?

598
00:38:58,566 --> 00:39:00,944
Me? I want fried chicken.

599
00:39:01,027 --> 00:39:03,196
-Just chicken? Not even omakase?
-So tasty.

600
00:39:08,159 --> 00:39:09,744
[both panting]

601
00:39:09,827 --> 00:39:12,288
-Tie it on nice and tight.
-Okay.

602
00:39:12,372 --> 00:39:14,248
I'll go up first and pull it up.

603
00:39:14,958 --> 00:39:16,209
-Be careful.
-Okay.

604
00:39:24,467 --> 00:39:25,593
[grunts]

605
00:39:25,677 --> 00:39:27,345
[panting]

606
00:39:33,893 --> 00:39:35,019
Give me a minute.

607
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:38,856
[♪ upbeat jazz music playing]

608
00:39:38,940 --> 00:39:41,150
-[gasps]
-[shushes]

609
00:39:45,822 --> 00:39:47,198
[gasps softly]

610
00:39:47,281 --> 00:39:48,282
[gun cocks]

611
00:39:49,158 --> 00:39:50,702
[exhales] The police.

612
00:39:50,785 --> 00:39:52,495
You came to arrest me.

613
00:39:54,872 --> 00:39:55,999
[exclaims]

614
00:39:58,584 --> 00:39:59,877
Hyeonsuk, I got it!

615
00:39:59,961 --> 00:40:01,087
I'll tie it up!

616
00:40:02,547 --> 00:40:04,716
[Isoo scatting]

617
00:40:07,343 --> 00:40:08,344
Be quiet.

618
00:40:09,470 --> 00:40:10,972
[Isoo humming]

619
00:40:13,224 --> 00:40:15,810
[Hyeonwoo] Hyeonsuk, did you open it?

620
00:40:19,731 --> 00:40:20,732
Come out.

621
00:40:22,191 --> 00:40:23,317
[exhales deeply]

622
00:40:35,371 --> 00:40:37,582
Don't even think about running.

623
00:40:37,665 --> 00:40:39,542
Where would you go anyway? Come here.

624
00:40:41,044 --> 00:40:42,045
Good job.

625
00:40:42,128 --> 00:40:43,796
[grunting]

626
00:40:44,505 --> 00:40:46,049
[grunting]

627
00:40:46,632 --> 00:40:48,342
I'm worn out from pulling that up,

628
00:40:48,426 --> 00:40:50,845
so you can cuff yourself.

629
00:40:50,928 --> 00:40:51,929
Thanks.

630
00:40:52,805 --> 00:40:54,348
What could this be?

631
00:40:54,432 --> 00:40:56,017
Put the cuffs on. It's okay.

632
00:40:59,062 --> 00:41:00,521
[latch rattling]

633
00:41:02,648 --> 00:41:03,649
[thuds]

634
00:41:10,782 --> 00:41:11,949
[lid creaks]

635
00:41:15,078 --> 00:41:16,120
[gasps]

636
00:41:16,204 --> 00:41:17,955
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

637
00:41:18,706 --> 00:41:20,666
What is it? Is it gold?

638
00:41:20,750 --> 00:41:22,418
Or diamonds?

639
00:41:23,753 --> 00:41:24,754
Do you want to know?

640
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:29,175
I'm not telling you.

641
00:41:29,258 --> 00:41:30,384
[sighs]

642
00:41:34,013 --> 00:41:35,014
[exclaims]

643
00:41:35,765 --> 00:41:36,766
Take them away.

644
00:41:45,983 --> 00:41:47,110
-[scoffs]
-[handcuffs click]

645
00:41:47,193 --> 00:41:48,820
[♪ suspenseful music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

646
00:41:56,369 --> 00:41:59,872
[Hyeonwoo] Our dad died of cancer
two years ago,

647
00:42:00,790 --> 00:42:03,459
and he left one final instruction.

648
00:42:04,335 --> 00:42:07,380
That house... [coughs, wheezes]

649
00:42:08,256 --> 00:42:10,216
You and your brother

650
00:42:11,509 --> 00:42:13,511
must get that house back.

651
00:42:15,263 --> 00:42:16,264
In that place...

652
00:42:18,516 --> 00:42:19,892
rests our family's

653
00:42:21,018 --> 00:42:24,480
most valuable possession.

654
00:42:26,774 --> 00:42:27,775
[whimpers]

655
00:42:28,484 --> 00:42:31,195
Just do as I say.

656
00:42:31,863 --> 00:42:32,864
[exhales sharply]

657
00:42:46,335 --> 00:42:47,753
We didn't believe him.

658
00:42:49,338 --> 00:42:53,009
But our relatives who came to the funeral
said something different.

659
00:42:53,676 --> 00:42:55,887
What happened to the treasure?

660
00:42:56,387 --> 00:42:57,388
Treasure?

661
00:42:58,973 --> 00:43:02,226
Father gave it to Hyeonwoo's grandfather,
didn't he?

662
00:43:02,310 --> 00:43:03,519
[elderly woman] Yes.

663
00:43:03,603 --> 00:43:05,104
That house.

664
00:43:05,188 --> 00:43:07,356
Father gave it to him.

665
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:09,483
The house? The house I was born in?

666
00:43:09,567 --> 00:43:11,986
[sighs] We sold that house years ago.

667
00:43:12,570 --> 00:43:13,946
That house has been sold.

668
00:43:14,030 --> 00:43:15,031
Yes, it's been sold.

669
00:43:16,657 --> 00:43:17,950
When you sold it,

670
00:43:18,492 --> 00:43:20,661
didn't you take out the chest?

671
00:43:20,745 --> 00:43:22,163
What chest?

672
00:43:22,747 --> 00:43:24,248
The treasure chest.

673
00:43:24,332 --> 00:43:28,044
[scoffs] Oh, come on. There's no treasure.

674
00:43:30,046 --> 00:43:31,672
Unless you saw it yourself...

675
00:43:31,756 --> 00:43:32,924
I saw it.

676
00:43:33,007 --> 00:43:35,426
I saw Father bury the chest there.

677
00:43:36,135 --> 00:43:37,511
You saw it too, didn't you?

678
00:43:38,012 --> 00:43:39,222
I did.

679
00:43:39,805 --> 00:43:42,016
In the dead of night,

680
00:43:42,099 --> 00:43:45,436
he secretly buried that chest
by the old well.

681
00:43:46,771 --> 00:43:49,565
It must've been awfully valuable.

682
00:43:50,316 --> 00:43:53,694
He said it should never be lost.

683
00:43:55,488 --> 00:43:59,492
But then a house was built there.

684
00:44:02,078 --> 00:44:04,330
Chairman Jin Myeongchul's house.

685
00:44:07,959 --> 00:44:09,585
What was inside that chest?

686
00:44:13,297 --> 00:44:14,882
Gold.

687
00:44:15,466 --> 00:44:18,761
I told your dad
when I went to visit him in the hospital.

688
00:44:18,844 --> 00:44:20,221
Nonsense.

689
00:44:20,304 --> 00:44:22,265
How many times do I have to tell you?

690
00:44:22,348 --> 00:44:23,975
You two were imagining things.

691
00:44:26,727 --> 00:44:27,812
[softly] Gold.

692
00:44:30,606 --> 00:44:33,442
Even then, I didn't believe it. But...

693
00:44:34,193 --> 00:44:36,487
Buy that house back, no matter the cost.

694
00:44:37,363 --> 00:44:39,532
The chest is still there.

695
00:44:39,615 --> 00:44:43,035
I need to get it
before those brats catch on.

696
00:44:43,119 --> 00:44:44,787
It was mine to begin with.

697
00:44:44,870 --> 00:44:46,080
Jackpot.

698
00:44:46,163 --> 00:44:48,666
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

699
00:44:49,250 --> 00:44:52,295
So, that's why you tried to kill me?

700
00:44:52,378 --> 00:44:54,797
[exclaims] We weren't trying to kill you.

701
00:44:54,880 --> 00:44:58,175
Yeah. We worked so hard
to make sure nobody got hurt.

702
00:44:58,259 --> 00:45:00,219
We set them off when no one was around.

703
00:45:00,303 --> 00:45:01,595
[♪ ominous music plays]

704
00:45:03,806 --> 00:45:05,641
I almost died three times.

705
00:45:05,725 --> 00:45:07,310
-That was all part of--
-[Hyeonwoo] Sorry.

706
00:45:07,393 --> 00:45:08,644
Sorry.

707
00:45:11,731 --> 00:45:12,732
But...

708
00:45:13,357 --> 00:45:15,401
could you just tell us one thing?

709
00:45:16,402 --> 00:45:17,987
What was inside the chest?

710
00:45:21,449 --> 00:45:23,909
We'll serve time, however many years.
So please.

711
00:45:23,993 --> 00:45:25,703
Please tell us just that. Please?

712
00:45:26,620 --> 00:45:27,663
Ah.

713
00:45:29,623 --> 00:45:30,750
Gold.

714
00:45:30,833 --> 00:45:31,876
[gasps]

715
00:45:33,336 --> 00:45:34,462
[breath trembles]

716
00:45:34,545 --> 00:45:35,880
How much was there?

717
00:45:36,464 --> 00:45:38,799
[exhales] Well, at today's gold prices,

718
00:45:38,883 --> 00:45:40,176
around 100 billion won?

719
00:45:40,259 --> 00:45:41,427
[both exclaim excitedly]

720
00:45:41,510 --> 00:45:42,595
[Hyeonwoo] 100 billion won?

721
00:45:44,221 --> 00:45:45,598
[cries joyfully]

722
00:45:50,936 --> 00:45:53,105
-That belongs to us, right?
-Of course, it does.

723
00:45:53,189 --> 00:45:54,398
Of course.

724
00:45:54,482 --> 00:45:56,692
You deserve it
after all you've been through.
STYLE
::cue()

725
00:45:56,776 --> 00:45:58,361
It should be a family heirloom.

726
00:45:58,444 --> 00:46:00,071
Can't you show it to us? Just once?

727
00:46:00,154 --> 00:46:01,489
We risked our lives for this.

728
00:46:01,572 --> 00:46:02,782
Please.

729
00:46:02,865 --> 00:46:05,993
It's ours anyway,
so please let us see it just once.

730
00:46:07,828 --> 00:46:09,580
[♪ jaunty music playing]

731
00:46:11,374 --> 00:46:12,458
Hmm.

732
00:46:17,963 --> 00:46:18,964
[grunts]

733
00:46:23,219 --> 00:46:26,597
You worked hard to find this treasure.
You should at least get to see it.

734
00:46:27,932 --> 00:46:29,433
All right.

735
00:46:33,104 --> 00:46:34,480
[both giggle excitedly]

736
00:46:35,648 --> 00:46:37,149
-Wow.
-We're rich now.

737
00:46:38,609 --> 00:46:40,486
-Wow.
-Wait, what is this?

738
00:46:41,028 --> 00:46:42,029
Wait, hold on.

739
00:46:42,113 --> 00:46:43,114
What?

740
00:46:51,163 --> 00:46:52,164
What the...

741
00:46:56,627 --> 00:46:57,628
[in English] Ready...

742
00:46:58,712 --> 00:46:59,713
Action.

743
00:47:00,214 --> 00:47:05,636
[in Korean] It was a treasure chest that
they orchestrated four bombings to get.

744
00:47:06,637 --> 00:47:09,932
What exactly was inside it?

745
00:47:10,015 --> 00:47:11,475
[♪ intriguing music playing]

746
00:47:12,726 --> 00:47:13,936
[creaking]

747
00:47:17,731 --> 00:47:20,067
The treasure they were
so desperate to find

748
00:47:21,610 --> 00:47:22,611
was none other than...

749
00:47:26,490 --> 00:47:28,242
"JANG DEUKSU"

750
00:47:28,325 --> 00:47:30,578
...a record of collaboration
with Imperial Japan.

751
00:47:33,497 --> 00:47:36,625
The bombers' great-grandfather
was Jang Deuksu.

752
00:47:36,709 --> 00:47:39,170
Also known as "The Master of Torture."

753
00:47:39,253 --> 00:47:43,215
He arrested and tortured
hundreds of independence activists

754
00:47:43,299 --> 00:47:45,301
as a pro-Japanese police officer.

755
00:47:45,384 --> 00:47:48,095
While working as an officer,

756
00:47:48,179 --> 00:47:51,724
Jang Deuksu threatened landowners
into handing over their deeds.

757
00:47:51,807 --> 00:47:54,477
These are those very documents.

758
00:47:55,394 --> 00:47:58,731
Jang Deuksu's sons, Kunkuk and Jongkuk,

759
00:47:59,482 --> 00:48:01,942
sold these lands, amassed a fortune,

760
00:48:02,026 --> 00:48:05,279
and went into postwar reconstruction,
which made them extremely wealthy.

761
00:48:06,113 --> 00:48:09,950
They believed their prosperity
would last forever,

762
00:48:11,243 --> 00:48:13,329
but then a troublemaker was born.

763
00:48:13,913 --> 00:48:16,624
Jang Jongkuk's only son
and the father of the bombers,

764
00:48:17,208 --> 00:48:21,587
Jang Myungjun,
failed at every business he tried.

765
00:48:22,505 --> 00:48:25,174
Perhaps this is what they call
justice prevailing.

766
00:48:25,257 --> 00:48:26,425
JUSTICE WILL PREVAIL

767
00:48:27,009 --> 00:48:28,427
But here's the thing.

768
00:48:30,179 --> 00:48:32,223
Before Jang Myungjun died of cancer,

769
00:48:32,306 --> 00:48:36,310
he told his sons to find the chest
their grandfather had left behind.

770
00:48:37,436 --> 00:48:39,438
The two fools who believed him

771
00:48:40,272 --> 00:48:44,401
orchestrated the bombings
to find this chest.

772
00:48:45,444 --> 00:48:46,862
But what they uncovered...

773
00:48:48,155 --> 00:48:49,323
was evidence

774
00:48:49,406 --> 00:48:53,911
that their family collaborated
with Imperial Japan during the occupation.

775
00:48:53,994 --> 00:48:57,498
It is truly a fitting end
for this collaborationist family.

776
00:48:58,666 --> 00:49:01,710
I suppose another name will be added
to the list of collaborators,

777
00:49:02,503 --> 00:49:04,964
which I plan to publish.

778
00:49:05,047 --> 00:49:08,384
This has been Jin Isoo,

779
00:49:09,385 --> 00:49:10,761
a detective for the people.

780
00:49:11,345 --> 00:49:13,013
[cheering]

781
00:49:13,097 --> 00:49:15,015
That's me. That's me, all right.

782
00:49:15,099 --> 00:49:16,475
A round of applause!

783
00:49:17,518 --> 00:49:19,311
What do you think? Amazing, right?

784
00:49:19,395 --> 00:49:20,604
Yes, amazing.

785
00:49:21,188 --> 00:49:22,773
The comments are blowing up.

786
00:49:23,357 --> 00:49:26,068
"Even busting collaborators,
what can't he do?"

787
00:49:26,151 --> 00:49:27,361
"Just how cool is he?"

788
00:49:28,112 --> 00:49:29,238
Wow, amazing.

789
00:49:29,321 --> 00:49:30,781
My God, just look at this.

790
00:49:30,864 --> 00:49:32,616
-Let's get a beer.
-Yes, sir.

791
00:49:32,700 --> 00:49:33,909
This is insane!

792
00:49:33,993 --> 00:49:35,869
-Look at this.
-Yes, you're amazing.

793
00:49:35,953 --> 00:49:37,997
-Look.
-[Junyoung] Come on. Let's go home.

794
00:49:38,080 --> 00:49:40,165
Where are you going? Come on, admire me.

795
00:49:40,249 --> 00:49:42,293
Bro, you're so cool. The best!

796
00:49:42,376 --> 00:49:43,711
Hey, let's go grab a beer.

797
00:49:43,794 --> 00:49:45,337
Sorry, I have a date.

798
00:49:45,421 --> 00:49:47,798
-Hello? Babe?
-Detective Park.

799
00:49:48,632 --> 00:49:49,633
I have plans, too.

800
00:49:49,717 --> 00:49:51,093
You don't have a girlfriend.

801
00:49:51,176 --> 00:49:53,429
Shut up. See you.

802
00:49:53,929 --> 00:49:55,180
Come on.

803
00:49:59,393 --> 00:50:00,477
[sighs softly]
STYLE
::cue()

804
00:50:08,527 --> 00:50:09,570
Jiwon.

805
00:50:09,653 --> 00:50:10,738
Surprised?

806
00:50:12,656 --> 00:50:14,283
Have you been waiting here for me?

807
00:50:14,366 --> 00:50:15,367
Yes.

808
00:50:15,451 --> 00:50:17,369
Come on, I found this great place to eat.

809
00:50:17,453 --> 00:50:19,413
There's always a long wait.
We should hurry.

810
00:50:20,664 --> 00:50:21,832
[Dr. Yoon chuckles]

811
00:50:21,915 --> 00:50:23,584
-Weren't you cold?
-I'm fine.

812
00:50:24,084 --> 00:50:26,128
Up for a drink again tonight?

813
00:50:26,962 --> 00:50:28,631
-[Junyoung] Sure.
-[Dr. Yoon] Great!

814
00:50:30,633 --> 00:50:31,800
[chuckles]

815
00:50:31,884 --> 00:50:33,802
I knew it.

816
00:50:35,137 --> 00:50:37,097
[sighs] I'm so lonely.

817
00:50:37,848 --> 00:50:40,934
I don't have anyone
to share this afterglow with.

818
00:50:44,772 --> 00:50:46,649
-Getting off work?
-Yes.

819
00:50:46,732 --> 00:50:49,068
Not sure if you saw the show,

820
00:50:49,151 --> 00:50:50,903
but I gave it one heck of an ending.

821
00:50:50,986 --> 00:50:52,363
[♪ quirky music playing]

822
00:50:52,446 --> 00:50:54,239
[Hyera] I didn't see it. I was too busy.

823
00:50:54,323 --> 00:50:55,949
Yes. Of course, you were.

824
00:50:57,201 --> 00:50:58,661
Guess this is goodbye.

825
00:50:58,744 --> 00:50:59,870
Happy?

826
00:50:59,953 --> 00:51:01,664
My face gives me away every time.

827
00:51:02,498 --> 00:51:05,709
Wishing you the best
with the Counterterrorism Team. Good luck.

828
00:51:06,293 --> 00:51:08,837
Right. You stay out of trouble, too.
Take care.

829
00:51:08,921 --> 00:51:09,922
Okay.

830
00:51:15,260 --> 00:51:16,762
[sighs in relief]

831
00:51:20,474 --> 00:51:21,934
[exhales deeply]

832
00:51:24,603 --> 00:51:25,771
[Changun] Joo.

833
00:51:26,730 --> 00:51:28,357
[in English] Would you like
something to drink?

834
00:51:30,359 --> 00:51:31,360
[in Korean] You did a great job.

835
00:51:32,069 --> 00:51:33,529
You too, sir.

836
00:51:35,572 --> 00:51:39,243
Working with you again
felt like old times.

837
00:51:39,326 --> 00:51:41,328
-[chuckles softly]
-I could really count on you.

838
00:51:41,412 --> 00:51:42,663
Me too.

839
00:51:43,539 --> 00:51:45,666
What did you think of Jin Isoo?

840
00:51:46,625 --> 00:51:47,751
[inhales deeply]

841
00:51:47,835 --> 00:51:49,670
He can be a bit odd,

842
00:51:50,629 --> 00:51:52,214
and he's unpredictable,

843
00:51:53,298 --> 00:51:54,967
but he's got good instincts.

844
00:51:55,050 --> 00:51:56,927
And he's quite serious about the job.

845
00:51:57,010 --> 00:51:58,470
Right?

846
00:51:58,554 --> 00:52:01,557
He's actually a decent detective.

847
00:52:02,891 --> 00:52:05,269
Do you have someone lined up
to lead Team 1?

848
00:52:08,230 --> 00:52:09,481
[inhales deeply]

849
00:52:09,565 --> 00:52:10,607
No. [exhales]

850
00:52:11,442 --> 00:52:12,443
No one.

851
00:52:17,281 --> 00:52:18,490
So I was wondering...

852
00:52:21,702 --> 00:52:22,786
[Isoo humming]

853
00:52:24,329 --> 00:52:26,874
Chief! Want to watch the show with me?

854
00:52:26,957 --> 00:52:28,333
I saw it.

855
00:52:28,417 --> 00:52:30,294
Jin Isoo, a detective for the people.

856
00:52:31,128 --> 00:52:34,131
Oh. You're getting a new team leader
on Monday.

857
00:52:34,214 --> 00:52:36,300
-Tell your team not to be late.
-Team leader?

858
00:52:36,383 --> 00:52:37,926
-Who is it?
-Curious?

859
00:52:38,010 --> 00:52:39,136
You bet.

860
00:52:39,720 --> 00:52:42,306
You'll see.
I brought in a solid detective.

861
00:52:44,516 --> 00:52:47,060
We're getting a new team leader?

862
00:52:47,978 --> 00:52:50,147
How very interesting.

863
00:52:52,274 --> 00:52:54,568
[on TV] I suppose another name will be
added to the list of collaborators,

864
00:52:55,319 --> 00:52:57,821
which I plan to publish.

865
00:52:58,405 --> 00:53:01,158
Apply now to receive yours for free.

866
00:53:02,242 --> 00:53:05,329
This has been Jin Isoo,

867
00:53:06,538 --> 00:53:07,915
a detective for the people.

868
00:53:07,998 --> 00:53:09,583
[chuckles softly]

869
00:53:09,666 --> 00:53:11,126
That nutjob.

870
00:53:12,252 --> 00:53:13,587
[chuckles softly]

871
00:53:18,175 --> 00:53:19,968
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

872
00:53:21,428 --> 00:53:22,930
[Isoo] Put it on.
STYLE
::cue()

873
00:53:23,013 --> 00:53:24,306
You didn't last time.

874
00:53:24,389 --> 00:53:26,141
Your head's on backward. That's it.

875
00:53:26,225 --> 00:53:27,768
Detective Park, wear it.

876
00:53:27,851 --> 00:53:30,395
-[whines]
-Very handsome. Perfect.

877
00:53:30,479 --> 00:53:31,480
Hello!

878
00:53:32,356 --> 00:53:33,857
[crowd cheering]

879
00:53:34,483 --> 00:53:36,485
[Isoo] Hi there! Want a photo?

880
00:53:36,568 --> 00:53:39,863
Okay. One, two, three.

881
00:53:40,364 --> 00:53:42,741
[Junyoung sighs]
He's going overboard again.

882
00:53:42,825 --> 00:53:44,451
[Kyungjin] Come on, it's all good fun.

883
00:53:45,452 --> 00:53:47,287
VIOLENT CRIME TEAM 1
NEW BOSS COMING

884
00:53:48,539 --> 00:53:50,791
Ahh! Post it on social media.

885
00:53:50,874 --> 00:53:52,084
Okay, band.

886
00:53:52,167 --> 00:53:53,168
Let's give it a try.

887
00:53:53,252 --> 00:53:55,003
Just like we practiced. Ready!

888
00:53:56,755 --> 00:53:57,840
[shouts command]

889
00:53:57,923 --> 00:54:00,092
[♪ triumphant brass fanfare playing]

890
00:54:08,642 --> 00:54:09,726
[in English] Stop!

891
00:54:09,810 --> 00:54:10,811
[in Korean] What in the world...

892
00:54:10,894 --> 00:54:12,271
WELCOME, OUR NEW TEAM LEADER

893
00:54:12,354 --> 00:54:14,189
What is all this?

894
00:54:14,273 --> 00:54:15,274
[in Korean] Sir!

895
00:54:16,567 --> 00:54:19,111
Oh, for heaven's sake.

896
00:54:20,487 --> 00:54:21,488
Sir.

897
00:54:22,072 --> 00:54:24,366
Come on, clear all this out.
[exclaims scornfully]

898
00:54:24,825 --> 00:54:25,826
-This was...
-Sir!

899
00:54:25,909 --> 00:54:26,910
Jin Isoo's doing.

900
00:54:26,994 --> 00:54:29,413
It's for my new boss. You know the drill.

901
00:54:30,205 --> 00:54:31,248
Oh.

902
00:54:34,543 --> 00:54:35,752
[chuckles]

903
00:54:35,836 --> 00:54:37,754
-Somebody's working hard.
-[Isoo] Of course.

904
00:54:37,838 --> 00:54:39,715
We're getting a new team leader.

905
00:54:39,798 --> 00:54:40,799
Of course.

906
00:54:40,883 --> 00:54:42,634
-Like the flowers?
-Yeah.

907
00:54:42,718 --> 00:54:45,554
-Oh. Incoming!
-Really? My new boss is here?

908
00:54:46,430 --> 00:54:49,099
[whispering] Okay, here we go.
[shouts command]

909
00:54:51,393 --> 00:54:52,519
[shouts command]

910
00:54:52,603 --> 00:54:54,771
[♪ triumphant brass fanfare playing]

911
00:55:09,036 --> 00:55:10,120
[engine shuts off]

912
00:55:13,582 --> 00:55:14,750
[music stops]

913
00:55:17,085 --> 00:55:19,087
[♪ dramatic music plays]

914
00:55:22,883 --> 00:55:24,593
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

915
00:55:27,846 --> 00:55:28,847
Joo Hyera?

916
00:55:38,190 --> 00:55:39,566
[camera shutters clicking]

917
00:56:07,219 --> 00:56:09,930
-[music fades]
-I didn't expect such a grand welcome.

918
00:56:10,013 --> 00:56:11,098
[chuckles softly]

919
00:56:11,765 --> 00:56:14,559
Detective Jin has been working hard
since morning.

920
00:56:15,477 --> 00:56:16,645
I guess you can be sweet.

921
00:56:17,604 --> 00:56:21,149
This is the new team leader of Violent
Crime Investigation Team 1, Joo Hyera.

922
00:56:22,401 --> 00:56:24,069
She's got years on you boys.

923
00:56:24,653 --> 00:56:27,739
She was on our Violent Crime Team
before moving to Counterterrorism.

924
00:56:27,823 --> 00:56:28,824
[chuckles softly]

925
00:56:28,907 --> 00:56:32,035
Detective Jin,
take good care of your new boss.

926
00:56:33,787 --> 00:56:34,913
Take good care of her.

927
00:56:39,918 --> 00:56:41,253
Detective Jin Isoo,

928
00:56:41,962 --> 00:56:44,715
Detective Park Junyoung,
Detective Choi Kyungjin...

929
00:56:44,798 --> 00:56:46,174
I'm glad to join the team.
STYLE
::cue()

930
00:56:48,218 --> 00:56:49,720
[muttering] This has to be a nightmare.

931
00:56:49,803 --> 00:56:50,846
It's real.

932
00:56:51,888 --> 00:56:53,181
Get used to it.

933
00:56:53,765 --> 00:56:55,767
[microphone feedback]

934
00:57:00,814 --> 00:57:02,816
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

935
00:57:03,942 --> 00:57:05,527
Looking forward to it, nutjob.

936
00:57:29,009 --> 00:57:30,260
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 2

937
00:57:30,343 --> 00:57:31,595
JIN ISOO AND JOO HYERA MEET AGAIN!

938
00:57:56,203 --> 00:57:59,623
Special Cast.
Kim Uiseong

939
00:58:06,713 --> 00:58:07,798
[Hyera] What's the report about?

940
00:58:07,881 --> 00:58:09,007
[woman] There's a ghost
in the abandoned house.

941
00:58:09,090 --> 00:58:11,551
It's asking us to catch the killer.

942
00:58:11,635 --> 00:58:12,928
Of course I'm not scared.

943
00:58:13,678 --> 00:58:14,971
There's definitely something in there.

944
00:58:15,055 --> 00:58:16,598
[man] You uncovered five bodies?

945
00:58:16,681 --> 00:58:18,558
-I said wait for the warrant.
-I bought the house!

946
00:58:18,642 --> 00:58:21,269
[man] A couple and their son,
a college student, were all murdered.

947
00:58:21,353 --> 00:58:24,105
So the house was abandoned after that,
and then it was used as a burial site.

948
00:58:24,189 --> 00:58:26,942
Police! Please come out, serial killer.

949
00:58:27,651 --> 00:58:29,027
[Hyera] We need to start this case over.

950
00:58:29,110 --> 00:58:31,530
-[muffled] Help me!
-[Isoo] So they're professional killers?

951
00:58:31,613 --> 00:58:33,406
[Hyera] They're methodical and cold.

952
00:58:33,490 --> 00:58:35,158
-There's something here.
-[Isoo] Detective Joo.

953
00:58:35,242 --> 00:58:36,368
Just stay close to me from now on.

954
00:58:36,451 --> 00:58:37,619
The hero never dies that easily.

955
00:58:37,702 --> 00:58:38,912
Meow.

956
00:58:39,913 --> 00:58:41,623
Jin Isoo! Nutjob!

957
00:58:41,706 --> 00:58:43,959
-Yes, ma'am!
-[Hyera] We don't know who attacked us.

958
00:58:44,042 --> 00:58:46,044
-Is there a fire?
-[Isoo] No one's going to die.

959
00:58:46,127 --> 00:58:47,212
Why are you being so dramatic?

960
00:58:47,295 --> 00:58:50,632
There's a fire. The detectives
went inside, but now it's on fire.

961
00:58:50,715 --> 00:58:52,092
How do we get out?

962
00:58:53,218 --> 00:58:55,929
-Hey, Jin Isoo.
-[Isoo] I'm working on it!

963
00:58:56,012 --> 00:58:57,097
Get out of the way.

964
00:59:01,226 --> 00:59:03,478
[♪ pensive music playing]

965
00:59:35,760 --> 00:59:37,304
DISSOLUTION

966
01:00:03,622 --> 01:00:05,624
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

